              <li style="display:flex; gap:10px; align-items:flex-start; font-size:var(--text-base); color:var(--gray-800);"><Icon name="circle-check" style="font-size:17px; color:var(--brand); margin-top:1px;" /> Split them, or bring your own PostgreSQL, when you need to</li>
              <li style="display:flex; gap:10px; align-items:flex-start; font-size:var(--text-base); color:var(--gray-800);"><Icon name="circle-check" style="font-size:17px; color:var(--brand); margin-top:1px;" /> Helm chart for Kubernetes, the same settings either way</li>
            </ul>
            <a class="btn-ghost" href="https://github.com/dmarc-analyzer-net/DmarcAnalyzerApp#readme" style="display:inline-flex; align-items:center; gap:8px; height:42px; padding:0 18px; border:1px solid var(--border-strong); border-radius:var(--radius-md); background:var(--surface-card); color:var(--text-body) !important; font-size:var(--text-base); font-weight:500;"><Icon name="book-open" style="font-size:16px;" /> Read the setup guide</a>
          </div>
          <Terminal
            lines={[
              { type: 'comment', text: '# fetch the compose file' },
              { type: 'cmd', text: 'curl -fsSL -o compose.yml https://…/deploy/compose.yml' },
              { type: 'gap' },
              { type: 'comment', text: '# key that encrypts stored mailbox passwords' },
              { type: 'cmd', text: 'echo "DMARC_ENCRYPTION_KEY=$(openssl rand -base64 32)" > .env' },
              { type: 'cmd', text: 'docker compose up -d' },
              { type: 'gap' },
              { type: 'ok', text: 'app      → http://localhost:8080' },
              { type: 'ok', text: 'postgres → localhost:5432' },
            ]}
